Reply Icon
1 Support Agent message

I'll help you understand how to download your project folder from Emergent to your local computer and open it in VS Code.

How to Download Your Project
Emergent offers two main ways to get your project code onto your computer:

Option 1: Save to GitHub (Recommended)
This is the best approach for managing your code:

Push your project to GitHub through the Emergent chat interface by asking the agent: "Please push this project to GitHub"
The agent will guide you through connecting your GitHub account if you haven't already
Clone the repository to your computer:
Open your terminal or command prompt
Run: git clone [your-repository-url
]
The repository URL will be provided after the push completes
Open in VS Code:
Launch VS Code
Go to File → Open Folder
Select the cloned project folder
Benefits of this method:

Version control for your code
Easy to sync updates between Emergent and your local environment
Professional workflow for ongoing development
You can continue working locally and push changes back
Option 2: Direct Code Download
If you need a quick one-time download:

In the Emergent chat interface, look for the download/export option (typically an icon or button in the interface)
Click to download the project as a ZIP file
Extract the ZIP file to a location on your computer
Open in VS Code:
Launch VS Code
Go to File → Open Folder
Select the extracted project folder
After Opening in VS Code
Once you have the project open locally:

Install any required dependencies (usually npm install or pip install -r requirements.txt depending on your project type)
Review the README file if one was generated for setup instructions
You can now edit, run, and test your project locally
Pro Tip: The GitHub method (Option 1) is strongly recommended because it allows you to save checkpoints, experiment with changes, and easily sync between Emergent and your local development environment.

