where are the pictures in public?

Nov 2,
02: 14 PM

The pictures are not currently inside public.

They are loaded from online Unsplash URLs in:

frontend/src/App.js
Look near the top for:

const images = {
  hero: "https://images.unsplash.com/...",
  korea: "https://images.unsplash.com/...",
};
Your public folder is here:

frontend/public/
To use local images:

Create this folder:
frontend/public/images/
Add your images there, for example:
hero.jpg
south-korea.jpg
dubai.jpg
Update App.js:
const images = {
  hero: "/images/hero.jpg",
  korea: "/images/south-korea.jpg",
  dubai: "/images/dubai.jpg",
};
Files inside public are referenced starting with /, not /public/.


