what should be in public foldr

Nov 2,
02: 26 PM

For this homepage, the public folder should contain the standard React files:

frontend/
└── public/
    ├── index.html
    ├── favicon.ico
    ├── logo192.png
    ├── logo512.png
    ├── manifest.json
    └── robots.txt
You can also create an images folder:

frontend/public/images/
Add your own images there if desired:

frontend/public/images/
├── hero.jpg
├── south-korea.jpg
├── dubai.jpg
├── london.jpg
└── canada.jpg
Then reference them in App.js like this:

const images = {
  hero: "/images/hero.jpg",
  korea: "/images/south-korea.jpg",
  dubai: "/images/dubai.jpg",
};
Important: write /images/hero.jpg, not /public/images/hero.jpg.

For the current version, no image files are required because the homepage uses online Unsplash images. The most important file in public is:

public/index.html

